{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and existing tests, make a focused fix, then run the tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nEvery request currently updates state when it finishes, even if a newer search has started. I’ll add a request counter and guard all completion updates; clearing the query will also advance the counter to invalidate pending requests.\n\nAll four existing tests pass. Since they don’t cover overlapping requests, I’ll also run an in-memory check for stale successes, stale failures, and requests finishing after the query is cleared, without changing any test files.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; 6 additional in-memory race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Commands exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; 6 additional in-memory race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Commands exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":15,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/4-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":199,"stdout_bytes":134,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-6b4917ca70936d17eb855f4250f78171.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"grep_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test; git diff --check; git diff --stat","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/4-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":298,"stdout_bytes":517,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-73bfd93997987d6c6c284971ea6d7712.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst item = title => [{ id: title, title, url: '/' }];\nfor (const staleFails of [false, true]) {\n  for (const order of ['old-first', 'new-first', 'clear']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (order === 'new-first') { requests[1].resolve(item('new')); await current; }\n    if (order === 'clear') await c.search('  ');\n    const expected = c.getState();\n    let emissions = 0;\n    const unsubscribe = c.subscribe(() => emissions++);\n    const before = emissions;\n    if (staleFails) requests[0].reject(new Error('stale'));\n    else requests[0].resolve(item('old'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n    assert.equal(emissions, before);\n    unsubscribe();\n    if (order !== 'new-first') { requests[1].resolve(item('new')); await current; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), order === 'clear'\n      ? { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null }\n      : { query: 'new', results: item('new'), loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('PASS: 6 overlapping-request and clear-query scenarios');\nNODE\n git diff --check","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/4-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":79,"stdout_bytes":54,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-7662e3856561c11d6e877e1b5d8db156.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":70434,"output_tokens":1208}}
